      "message": "From the spec in `18.2.4 Power Management messages`\n\n\u003e The SPMD denies a request from the SPMC to switch to the Normal world during message processing.\n\nMaybe we should introduce `SpmcState::PsciHandling` or something similar, so we can have `handle_secure_call_psci()` that gets called while a PSCI message processing is in progress. This could limit the message types accepted by the SPMD, and ensure that in never returns to NWd while in this state. @imre.kis@arm.com?",
